/P 181 0 R
/T (What has stayed with me is that these questions are not being asked by educators who do not care about child safety. In most cases, it is the complete opposite. They are being asked by educators who care so deeply about doing the right thing that they have started second guessing interactions that once felt natural, responsive and connected.)
/E (What has stayed with me is that these questions are not being asked by educators who do not care about child safety. In most cases, it is the complete opposite. They are being asked by educators who care so deeply about doing the right thing that they have started second guessing interactions that once felt natural, responsive and connected.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 181 0 R
/T (I can understand why this is happening, particularly when child safety conversations have become stronger, policies are being reviewed and educators are hearing more about boundaries, appropriate conduct and the importance of protecting children from harm. These conversations are necessary, and I would never want us to move away from them, but I also think there is another conversation that needs to sit alongside them.)
/E (I can understand why this is happening, particularly when child safety conversations have become stronger, policies are being reviewed and educators are hearing more about boundaries, appropriate conduct and the importance of protecting children from harm. These conversations are necessary, and I would never want us to move away from them, but I also think there is another conversation that needs to sit alongside them.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
