219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 181 0 R
/T (A three year old who is crying at drop off does not understand legislation or the nervousness an educator may now be feeling about whether they should offer physical comfort. They are communicating something through their body, their facial expression, their movement and sometimes through reaching towards the adult they trust, and our role is to become better at noticing what that child is communicating rather than becoming so frightened of making a mistake that we stop responding altogether.)
/E (A three year old who is crying at drop off does not understand legislation or the nervousness an educator may now be feeling about whether they should offer physical comfort. They are communicating something through their body, their facial expression, their movement and sometimes through reaching towards the adult they trust, and our role is to become better at noticing what that child is communicating rather than becoming so frightened of making a mistake that we stop responding altogether.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
