226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 182 0 R
/T (As you work through this guide, I would love you to think about the children in your own setting and notice the different ways they ask adults for connection. Some will reach their arms towards you, some will move closer without saying anything, some will ask directly for a cuddle, while others may become louder, busier or more physical when what they are really struggling to communicate is that they no longer feel settled or safe.)
/E (As you work through this guide, I would love you to think about the children in your own setting and notice the different ways they ask adults for connection. Some will reach their arms towards you, some will move closer without saying anything, some will ask directly for a cuddle, while others may become louder, busier or more physical when what they are really struggling to communicate is that they no longer feel settled or safe.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
