/E (A child might run towards an educator for a hug at drop off. Another might climb onto a familiar adult's lap after becoming overwhelmed. One child might need more space and very little physical contact, while another may move their whole body closer when they are tired, frightened or unsure. A child who has fallen may reach both arms towards the educator they trust, and another child may become louder or more physical when what they are really struggling to communicate is that they need help to feel settled again.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
