/P 193 0 R
/E (When people hear the words inappropriate touch, it is easy for the mind to jump straight to the worst possible interpretation, but in everyday early childhood practice the more useful question is often not simply whether physical contact happened, but whether that contact was necessary, respectful, appropriate for the child and connected to a genuine need in that moment.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
