>>
endobj
355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (For me, this is where context matters so much, because two interactions can look similar from a distance while having very different purposes.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (A child who has fallen and moves towards an educator for a brief cuddle is very different from an adult repeatedly encouraging physical closeness that the child has not sought. Helping a child move away from an immediate danger is very different from physically controlling them because they are not complying quickly enough, and sitting beside a distressed child who has moved close to you is very different from continuing physical contact once that child has started pulling away.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
