/P 196 0 R
/E (By this point in the guide, I hope you are beginning to feel that safe and appropriate touch is not about memorising a long list of rules, because in real early childhood settings there is rarely time to mentally work through a policy document while a child is crying at drop off, hiding under a table, reaching towards you for comfort, or becoming so overwhelmed that safety is suddenly at risk.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (What we do need is a simple way to slow our thinking down just enough that our response becomes thoughtful rather than automatic, and the easiest way I have found to do that is to pause, notice and respond.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
