393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (Pausing does not mean standing back and doing nothing, particularly when there is an immediate safety concern. It simply means giving ourselves a small moment to become aware of our own reaction before we move in, because when an educator is feeling rushed, worried, frustrated or frightened of getting something wrong, it is very easy to respond from our own nervous system rather than from what the child actually needs.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (Sometimes that pause might only be one breath, softening our shoulders, lowering our voice, or noticing that our own body has started to tense before we respond.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
