/P 197 0 R
/E (For me, that is where confidence starts to return, because we no longer need to choose between being frightened of touch and going back to doing things simply because that is how we have always done them. We can pause, notice the child in front of us, and make the most thoughtful decision we can in that moment. That is what safe, responsive practice looks like to me.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
