865 0 obj
<<
/Title (Over the past year, I have found myself having more and more conversations with early childhood educators who are trying incredibly hard to keep children safe, follow changing expectations and make thoughtful decisions in moments that often happen very quickly, yet underneath those conversations I keep hearing the same uncertainty coming through.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 771 0 R
/Next 1174 0 R
>>
endobj
866 0 obj
<<
/Title (A three year old who is crying at drop off does not understand legislation or the nervousness an educator may now be feeling about whether they should offer physical comfort. They are communicating something through their body, their facial expression, their movement and sometimes through reaching towards the adult they trust, and our role is to become better at noticing what that child is communicating rather than becoming so frightened of making a mistake that we stop responding altogether.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 771 0 R
/Prev 1175 0 R
>>
endobj
