/Title (I can understand why this is happening, particularly when child safety conversations have become stronger, policies are being reviewed and educators are hearing more about boundaries, appropriate conduct and the importance of protecting children from harm. These conversations are necessary, and I would never want us to move away from them, but I also think there is another conversation that needs to sit alongside them.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 771 0 R
/Prev 2225 0 R
/Next 1175 0 R
>>
endobj
2214 0 obj
<<
/Title (As you work through this guide, I would love you to think about the children in your own setting and notice the different ways they ask adults for connection. Some will reach their arms towards you, some will move closer without saying anything, some will ask directly for a cuddle, while others may become louder, busier or more physical when what they are really struggling to communicate is that they no longer feel settled or safe.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 867 0 R
/Prev 1176 0 R
/Next 2226 0 R
>>
endobj
2215 0 obj
<<
/Title (My hope is that it gives educators and leaders a calmer place to have these conversations together, so that instead of each person privately wondering whether they are getting it right, teams can begin building a shared understanding of what safe, responsive and respectful support can look like in everyday practice.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 867 0 R
/Prev 2226 0 R
/Next 1177 0 R
>>
endobj
2216 0 obj
<<
